    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P><STRONG><IMG src="/images/2005/stefani_sanremo.jpg" align=right border=0>Gwen Stefani</STRONG> - guest-star at the <STRONG>55th Sanremo Festival</STRONG> - unexpectedly made her entry in the press room yesterday, just few minutes before the show started. </P>
<P>She answered the questions of the Italian and International journalists that confronted her with <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>. <STRONG>"There's one and only Madonna," stated Gwen</STRONG>. She also said that she esteem and appreciate <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> more today than when she [Gwen] was a teenager.</P>
<P>"When her success started, in the 80's, I was only 15 years old and I was still attending the high school. At that time I didn't like pop music, but I liked ska. Only later I realized that her music would have stayed in my memory. I have to admit that in my own album I really wanted to follow that sound. <STRONG>But a new Madonna doesn't exist. She marked out a new road, not only for women but also for a lot of men</STRONG>."</P>
</font></div>
