  <tr>
    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=5">Movies</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>Pennies for the Guy.</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P>Mar 4 2005 Karen Price, Western Mail </P>
<P>He's no stranger to working with big names, but <STRONG>Welsh actor Andrew Howard</STRONG> stepped into a different league when<STRONG> Madonna's</STRONG> director hubby<STRONG> Guy Ritchie asked him to appear in his new movie</STRONG>. Karen Price caught up with him. ANDREW Howard is the first to admit he has an interesting life. When he's not dining with Hollywood stars like Glenn Close, <STRONG>he's playing chess with director Guy Ritchie. The Welsh actor has just finished filming Ritchie's latest movie, Revolver</STRONG>. As with Ritchie's previous films - Snatch and Lock, Stock and Two Smoking Barrels - Revolver is your typical action picture, featuring some of the hottest young actors. But in between takes, any thoughts of partying were banished as they took part in far more leisurely pursuits. "There were lots of games of chess on set," says Howard. "Guy was pretty good, although I think we eventually reached stalemate." <STRONG>Revolver, which is due to be released this summer</STRONG>, was shot on the Isle of Man and in London. It is set in the casino world and focuses on Jake (Jason Statham), a hotshot gambler, who takes on a local crime boss and casino owner. Howard plays Jake's brother. "It was a good experience and Guy was great to work with," says the 34-year-old. "I have a lot of time for him as he was very relaxed and chilled and you felt no pressure. "He was also very open to suggestions. "It's a nice role. I like the style of Guy's movies. I think they are really entertaining films. I'm excited to be in a Guy Ritchie movie - it's cool." <STRONG>But Cardiff-born Howard didn't get the opportunity to meet the director's superstar wife Madonna. "Madonna was around but I didn't get to meet her as the day she was on set I was filming a big emotional scene. But she seemed very nice."</STRONG> </P>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
